## Linux Kernel Audit Rules (auditd) - Assume Breach Honeytoken Telemetry
##
## Monitors read (r), write (w), and attribute change (a) syscalls on the
## decoy database credentials file. Execute (x) is intentionally omitted since
## .env files are configuration artifacts rather than executable binaries.

-w /opt/clinica/datos/pacientes_db_credenciales.env -p rwa -k honeytoken_acceso
